      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. VII.—एकान्तगुण. The commentary is somewhat obscure. It",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "says एकान्तगुणरहस्यं तदेव मौनम्—एकान्त means certain, invariable.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Comp. Raghuvans′a II. 57. For the use of गुण comp. Mâgha",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "XVI., 42. On गुण Râmarshi adds मौनिनो निरपरीक्षित्त्वात् which is not",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "quite correct.—Âkhyânakî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. VIII.—I am inclined to take यदा कि° as equal to यदा अकि°",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "to mark distinctly the contrast with the third line. The com-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "mentary says किंचिज्ज्ञोहमपि किंचिञ्जानामीति द्विप इव करीव मदान्धःसमभवम्.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "But किंचिज्ज्ञ refers, I think, not to the speaker’s estimate of him-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "self at the time of his ‘blindness,’ but to the fact as he sees it",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "after his ‘intoxication’ has left him. The commentary does, I",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "think, some violence to the original. The double meaning of मद",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "will be noted. The last line is much condensed and requires",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "words to be supplied.—S′ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. IX.—This Stanza occurs also in the S′ântis′ataka see Kâvya-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "sangraha p. 307. शङ्कते = has any fear, or misgiving (i. e. that he is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "doing anything mean) अस्मदीयोयमिति मन्यते says Râmarshi. This does",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "not seem to be correct. On the reading विशङ्कते, Râmarshi says,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "न विश्वसिति एतद्ग्रहीष्यतीति मन्यते इत्यर्थः, परिग्रहः = that which is accepted or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "possessed.—Hâriṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. X.—अथवा is equivalent to “no wonder.” In this sense",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the expression is a common one. Comp. Mâlatî-Mâdhava p. 115.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "(Bombay Sans. Classics) Kâvyâdars′a II., St. 121, and the gloss",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "on it, or Uttararâmacharita p. 142. The idea of this Stanza ap-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "parently shocks the commentator’s orthodoxy and he says अयं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "गङ्गादृष्टान्तो युक्तो नैव तथापि एकदेशी पतनार्थमुक्तः.[*] But Gangâ is described",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "as having become arrogant in the Râmâyaṇa (Bâlakâṇḍa XLIII.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "6. Bomb. Ed.) विशाम्यहं हि पातालं स्रोतसा गृह्य शंकरम् । तस्यावलेपनं ज्ञात्वा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "क्रुद्धस्तु भगवान्हरः ॥ &c. The commentator’s explanation of the third",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
